( C72 {F4 T6f, 2026-10-13} nodal stress output on a mesh fixed in space with convection_apply -yes. 40 quad4 strip 10 x 1, elastic {young 1, poisson 0}, uniform velx 1 {inlet + initial node_dof}, so the strain rate is zero; initial sigzz = sin^2 pulse on 1 <= x <= 3. Neither code convects the integration-point stress, and the Professional 02-08-2026 nodal stress is the recovery of the integration-point stress: the pulse stays frozen, post_point sigzz at x = 1.5 / 2.0 / 2.5 = 0.5 / 1.0 / 0.5 at t = 2 {Professional run with global_element_dof_from_node_dof -yes, the Professional keyword that starts the integration points from node_dof, which GNU did by default before C100}. Before C72 GNU transported the nodal stress incrementally with a lumped mass weight F/volume against a convective weight h, so the pulse moved at about v*volume_ip {0.055}: 0.348732 / 0.6481 at x = 1.5 / 2.5. )

echo -no
number_of_space_dimensions 2
materi_velocity
materi_stress
end_initia
mesh -fixed_in_space -fixed_in_space
inertia_apply -no
convection_apply -yes
